.TH "libnvme_alloc_huge" 9 "libnvme_alloc_huge" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvme_alloc_huge \- Allocate a huge page-backed memory buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void *" libnvme_alloc_huge
.BI "(size_t len "  ","
.BI "struct libnvme_mem_huge *mh "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "len" 12
Size of the memory buffer in bytes
.IP "mh" 12
Huge memory allocation descriptor
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Attempts to allocate a memory buffer backed by huge pages. Allocation
details are stored in \fImh\fP and must later be released using
\fBlibnvme_free_huge\fP.
.SH "RETURN"
pointer to the allocated memory buffer on success, or NULL on
failure.
